      "summary": "A race between the basis check and decision commit can record a decision against an obsolete basis when the request supplies the revision reached by the concurrent update. The existing stale-basis test does not cover this interleaving.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Reviews/TechnicalReviewEndpoints.cs",
          "line": 79,
          "message": "Recheck the basis inside the atomic commit. A concurrent basis update can otherwise let a decision against an obsolete basis be recorded.",
          "confidence": 0.87,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "RecordDecision reads the current basis, validates it, then commits using only body.ExpectedRevision. CaseStateStore.Commit checks the revision but does not recheck that the basis in the decision detail is still current.",
            "failureScenario": "If the request predicts the next revision, a basis update can commit after the basis read and before this decision commit. The decision then succeeds and is audited against the old basis, despite that basis no longer being current."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
